  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n (3y+(3)/(y))=8\n\n**Concept used:**\n\nIf x + 1/x = P then,\n\nx² + (1/x²) = P² - 2\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n (3y+(3)/(y))=8\n\n⇒ 3 × {y + (1/y)} = 8\n\n⇒ {y + (1/y)} = 8/3\n\n⇒ {y² + (1/y²)} = (8/3)² - 2\n\n⇒ {y2 + (1/y2)} = (64/9) - 2\n\n⇒ {y2 + (1/y2)} = (64 - 18)/9\n\n⇒ {y2 + (1/y2)} = 46/9 = 5(1)/(9) \n\n**∴ The correct answer is 5(1)/(9).**",
